xing)        echo \"fixing\" ;;\n    ready-for-pr)  echo \"ready-for-pr\" ;;\n    pr-created)    echo \"pr-created\" ;;\n    testing)       echo \"testing\" ;;\n    reviewing)     echo \"reviewing\" ;;\n    rejected)      echo \"rejected\" ;;\n    merged|idle)   echo \"\" ;;\n    *)             echo \"\" ;;\n  esac\n}\n```\n\nThis function maps backend IssueStatus constants to GitHub labels. The `_sync_github_label()` function uses this mapping to automatically add/remove labels when statuses change.\n\n## 2. Label Initialization (`D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\.claude\\skills\\003-1-issue-init/scripts/init.sh`)\n\nThe init script reads `labels.conf` and creates GitHub labels:\n\n```bash\n# 逐行读取标签定义并创建\ncreated=0\nskipped=0\nwhile IFS='|' read -r name color desc; do\n  # 跳过空行和注释\n  [[ -z \"$name\" || \"$name\" == \\#* ]] && continue\n  # 去除前后空格\n  name=$(echo \"$name\" | xargs)\n  color=$(echo \"$color\" | xargs)\n  desc=$(echo \"$desc\" | xargs)\n\n  if gh label create \"$name\" --color \"$color\" --description \"$desc\" --force &>/dev/null; then\n    created=$((created + 1))\n    skill_log \"INFO\" \"[init] 标签已创建: $name\"\n  else\n    skipped=$((skipped + 1))\n    skill_log \"WARN\" \"[init] 标签创建失败或已存在: $name\"\n  fi\ndone < \"$LABELS_CONF\"\n```\n\n**Key point**: Label names are used exactly as-is from `labels.conf` after trimming whitespace. There's no transformation or validation.\n\n## 3. All IssueStatus Constants (`D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\internal\\backend\\domain\\issue.go`)\n\n```go\nconst (\n    IssueIdle       IssueStatus = \"idle\"        // 空闲，无人领取\n    IssueClaimed    IssueStatus = \"claimed\"     // 已被某 session 领取\n    IssueFixing     IssueStatus = \"fixing\"      // 正在开发中\n    IssueReadyForPR IssueStatus = \"ready-for-pr\" // 开发完成，等待提 PR\n    IssuePRCreated  IssueStatus = \"pr-created\"  // PR 已创建\n    IssueTesting    IssueStatus = \"testing\"     // 测试中\n    IssueReviewing  IssueStatus = \"reviewing\"   // 审核中\n    IssueMerged     IssueStatus = \"merged\"      // 已合并（终态）\n    IssueRejected   IssueStatus = \"rejected\"    // 被打回\n)\n```\n\n## 4. Label Usage in 003-* Skills\n\nThe following label queries are used in the scripts:\n\n### 003-4-issue-claim:\n- Lists issues: `--label \"in-progress\"` \n- Manual claim command: `--add-label \"in-progress\"`\n- Manual reject command: `--remove-label \"rejected\"`\n\n### 003-5-issue-fix:\n- Lists issues: `--label \"in-progress\"`\n\n### 003-6-issue-done:\n- Manual command: `--remove-label \"in-progress\" --add-label \"ready-for-pr\"`\n\n### 003-7-issue-pr:\n- Lists issues: `--label \"ready-for-pr\"`\n\n### 003-9-issue-review:\n- Manual reject command: `--remove-label \"in-progress\" --add-label \"rejected\"`\n\n## 5. Label Validation\n\n**There is NO validation code** that checks labels against `labels.conf`. The system:\n\n1. Creates labels from `labels.conf` in 003-1-issue-init\n2. Uses hardcoded label names in queries throughout the 003-* skills\n3. Uses the `_status_to_label()` function to automatically manage status labels\n\nThe workflow assumes that:\n- Labels are initialized first using 003-1-issue-init\n- All subsequent operations use the exact label names as defined in `labels.conf`\n- No validation occurs before using labels in operations\n\n## Summary of Label Flow:\n\n1. **Initialization**: `labels.conf` defines all available labels\n2. **Status Changes**: Backend status → `_status_to_label()` → GitHub label add/remove\n3. **Querying**: Skills use hardcoded label names like \"in-progress\", \"ready-for-pr\" etc.\n4. **No Validation**: The system trusts that labels exist as defined in `labels.conf`\n\nThe label system relies on proper initialization and consistent naming rather than runtime validation."}]}]}
